=== kill -STOP and -CONT on a job
stop rc=0
[1]+  Stopped                 sleep 3
cont rc=0
[1]+  Running                 sleep 3 &
killed 143
=== by PID, -TSTP and a pipeline
[1]+  Stopped                 sleep 3 | sleep 3
[1]+  Running                 sleep 3 | sleep 3 &
pipeline gone
=== a stopped job does not outlive its shell
ended with the shell
=== kill -l lists the job signals
1
